## STEP-00 confirmation

HUMAN confirmed via `ask_user_question:confirm-control-plane-redesign-scope`: freeze current execution; design systemic control-plane/pre-charge admission; council-review exact design bytes; do not build or execute a WBS in this AIP.

## Failure model

### Systemic root cause — RC-SYSTEM-01

The mission has no single atomic, mechanically closed **pre-charge admission transaction** covering all execution-control surfaces. Plan schema/hash approval is checked separately from strict execution-ledger validity, AIP/ASC transition capability, command-backend availability, reviewer capacity, Team-plan authority, goal activation and budget contingency. Consequently a charge can be committed while one or more mandatory downstream controls are invalid or unavailable.

This produces the observed loop:

```text
partial preflight → charge → mutate one control surface → discover another invalid surface
→ block review/acceptance → pause → re-plan → consume another reconciliation charge
```

The root cause is a control-architecture defect. Runner architecture, sandbox refusal, reviewer failure, stale ASC and ledger incompatibility are contributing failures or symptoms, not competing root causes.

